 "result": "Three failing tests are not caused by the Werkzeug 3.0.3 `partitioned` cookie problem, plus one teardown error that follows from it. One of the three is a judgment call, since it is still a Werkzeug version issue.\n\n1. **`test_request.py::test_limit_config`**: it expects `max_form_memory_size == 500_000` but gets `None`. It is still caused by the old Werkzeug (3.0.3 defaults that attribute to `None`, 3.1 to 500_000), but it is a different attribute and code path (`src/tessel/wrappers.py:93-111`) from the cookie `TypeError`.\n\n2. **`test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`**: it raises `RuntimeError: Install Tessel with the 'async' extra in order to use async views` (`src/tessel/app.py:1096`). `asgiref` is not installed. This is unrelated to Werkzeug.\n\n3. **`test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`**: it failed in the full run but passes when run alone, and it did not reproduce in a later full run. The source logic (`app.py:435-436`) looks correct. The subagent's guess is a leaked resource from another failing test being reported as an unraisable warning, but that is unverified.\n\nThe teardown error on `test_stream_keeps_session` is a leaked app context from the same `TypeError`, so it is not independent of the main cause. It is counted separately only because it shows up as an error rather than a failure.",
